### Example 1 — Community Marketplace Web App

**Scope summary**
A neighbourhood marketplace where residents list second-hand items, message sellers, and
arrange pickup. Scope covers user profiles, listing CRUD with photo uploads, in-app
messaging, and email notifications. Mobile-responsive web only; no native apps in v1.

**Effort and cost**
Discovery and UX design consume the first two weeks, focusing on trust signals (verified
profiles, report listing) and a frictionless posting flow. Backend work centres on
PostgreSQL data modelling, image storage on S3, and a WebSocket messaging layer; this is
the largest cost driver at roughly 90 hours. The responsive frontend adds another 70
hours across listing browse, detail, chat, and profile screens. Testing and a soft launch
with one pilot neighbourhood account for the remaining 30 hours. Total effort is about 210
hours, approximately 13,000 EUR at standard developer rates.

**Team and timeline**
A full-stack lead and a part-time designer pair for ten weeks. The designer fronts loads
in weeks 1–3; the developer carries implementation through week 9 with QA and bug fixing
in week 10.

**Risks and assumptions**
Moderation tooling is manual in v1 (admin ban only). Payment processing is explicitly out
of scope. Assumes fewer than 5,000 active listings at launch.

