### Example 2 — University Research Grant Management System

**Scope summary**
A SaaS module for university research offices to publish grant calls, collect applicant
submissions with budget breakdowns, run committee review scoring, and export award letters.
Supports multi-faculty tenancy, SSO via institutional SAML, and PDF generation for legal
review. English and Spanish UI required.

**Effort and cost**
Discovery includes compliance workshops (GDPR, public procurement thresholds) and committee
workflow mapping across three faculties—approximately 40 hours. Bilingual UX design and a
component library for forms-heavy screens consume 56 designer hours.

The submission portal with dynamic budget templates, file uploads up to 50 MB, and
validation rules is the largest single workstream at 100 developer hours. Review committee
scoring (blinded rounds, conflict-of-interest declarations, aggregate ranking) adds 80 hours.
SAML SSO integration with test IdP environments is 32 hours. PDF award letter generation with
merge fields and digital-signature placeholders is 40 hours. Reporting for research office
leadership (funnel metrics, award rate by faculty) is 36 hours.

Automated test coverage for scoring edge cases, accessibility audit remediation, and
load testing for deadline-day traffic spikes (3× normal) account for 72 hours. Documentation,
admin training webinars, and staged faculty rollout add 40 hours. Total effort is about 496
hours, roughly 30,500 EUR.

**Team and timeline**
One technical lead, two full-stack developers, one designer, and a QA engineer from week 10.
Delivery spans 20 weeks with faculty pilots in weeks 16–18 and general availability in week 20.

**Risks and assumptions**
Assumes SAML metadata is provided by week 4; late IdP changes have caused two-week slips on
similar projects. Committee scoring rules are frozen after discovery—mid-project rule changes
are change-order scope. Spanish translations are client-reviewed; engineering supplies i18n
framework only. Peak submission traffic may require read-replica provisioning not included
in base estimate.

